    "sentence_translations": [
      "Come Out For A Stroll",
      "",
      "One day, Lili was just having a coffee at a cafe when she received a phone call from Little Yu:",
      "“Hello, come out for a stroll?”",
      "",
      "Lili didn’t want to go out, so she said: “I’m sick and sleeping.”",
      "",
      "Little Yu didn’t say anything. After a few seconds, Little Yu said: “Look to your left.”",
      "",
      "Lili looked to the left only to see Little Yu standing outside the cafe window holding her phone.",
      "",
      "Lili felt really embarrassed.",
      "It turns out that Little Yu’s invitation to “Come out for a stroll?” was just that she wanted to greet Lili.",
      "Just like people often greet each other saying “Have you eaten?” or “Where are you going?” when they meet.",
      "She wasn’t really asking Lili to come out with her.",
      ""
